// Reactivity S4 — an effect that changes a signal it depends on is a self-reinforcing cycle: every run
// re-dirties the signal, which re-queues the effect, with no value-equality suppression to ever stop
// it. The scheduler bounds each flush (MAX_FLUSH_STEPS) and surfaces this as a runtime error rather than
// hanging (or, without the coalescing fix, overflowing the stack). Both backends bound at the same step
// count, so the abort is deterministic and differential-identical.
// expect: error E0045 at 9:1
// expect: exit 1
count = signal(0)
effect(fn() {
    count.set(count.get() + 1)
})
